        "original_id": "2f576441-a66a-56ca-bbb3-2c12f961461b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Matthew Bailes, Houman Younessi\n- Organizations: Swinburne University of Technology, Centre for Astrophysics and Supercomputing, OzGrav, ARC Centre of Excellence for Gravitational Wave Discovery, University of Connecticut, Hartford Graduate Campus of Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute\n- Places: Melbourne, Victoria, Hawthorn, Kew, Hartford, Connecticut, Australia\n- Infrastructure: East Kew railway station, Outer Circle railway line\n\nFacts:\n- In 1997, Houman Younessi attained tenure at Swinburne University of Technology in Hawthorn, Victoria, Australia.\n- Houman Younessi was later a member of the faculty at Swinburne University of Technology, then head of faculty and professor at the Hartford Graduate Campus of Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute in Hartford, Connecticut, and then a research professor at the University of Connecticut.\n- Swinburne University of Technology is an Australian public university based in Melbourne, Victoria.\n- Swinburne University of Technology has its main campus in Hawthorn, a suburb of Melbourne 7.5 km from the Melbourne central business district.\n- Matthew Bailes is an astrophysicist at the Centre for Astrophysics and Supercomputing at Swinburne University of Technology.\n- Matthew Bailes is the Director of OzGrav, the ARC Centre of Excellence for Gravitational Wave Discovery.\n- East Kew railway station was a railway station on the Outer Circle railway line in Kew, Melbourne, Victoria, Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d333973f-aa4f-5bfb-af6c-a386727b4c66",
        "text": "Page: Matthew Bailes. Sentence: Professor Matthew Bailes is an astrophysicist at the Centre for Astrophysics and Supercomputing, Swinburne University of Technology and the Director of OzGrav, the ARC Centre of Excellence for Gravitational Wave Discovery.\nPage: Swinburne University of Technology. Sentence: Swinburne University of Technology (often simply called Swinburne) is an Australian public university based in Melbourne, Victoria.\nPage: Swinburne University of Technology. Sentence: Its main campus is located in Hawthorn, a suburb of Melbourne which is located 7.5 km from the Melbourne central business district.\nPage: Houman Younessi. Sentence: He was a research professor at University of Connecticut, and was previously the head of faculty and professor at Hartford Graduate Campus of Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute in Hartford, Connecticut and prior to that, a member of the faculty at Swinburne University of Technology in Hawthorn, Victoria, Australia where he attained tenure in 1997.\nPage: East Kew railway station. Sentence: East Kew was a railway station on the Outer Circle railway line, located in the suburb of Kew, Melbourne, Victoria, Australia.",
